  m_Name: balancing
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GameTerms.Runtime::GameTerms.GlossaryTermAsset
  data:
    Id: balancing
    Term: Balancing
    Abbreviation: 
    Category: 0
    Difficulty: 1
    ShortDefinition: Tuning numbers and rules so options remain viable without a
      single dominant strategy.
    SimpleExplanation: Adjusting systems so no weapon, character, or tactic wins
      every time.
    WhyItMatters: Balance protects fairness, variety, and long-term engagement.
    Example: Nerfing an overused rifle while buffing underplayed shotguns after telemetry
      review.
    CommonMistake: Balancing based only on top-player complaints without looking
      at overall usage data.
    PracticePrompt: Pick three competing options and chart win rate and pick rate
      after twenty playtests.
    GameUses:
    - Combat systems
    - Economy design
    - Live ops patches
    RelatedTermIds:
    - difficulty-curve
    - risk-reward
    - economy-design
    - a-b-testing
    Tags:
    - balance
    - tuning
    - systems
    Synonyms: []
